UPDATE dbo.SessionTranscripts SET Transcript = '<h2>The Purpose of Messengers: A Call to Awaken from Heedlessness</h2>
<p class="mainText">Impurity arises from filth ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ù†Ø¬Ø§Ø³Øª</span>). The transition from a state of impurity to one of purity is called <span class="inlineArabic">Ø·Ù‡Ø§Ø±Ø©</span> (purification). Since a human being is a composition of both the body and the soul ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ù†ÙØ³</span>), purifying the soul is as essential as purifying the body. Physical purity is achieved through the performance of outward religious acts, whereas the purification of the soul is attained by acquiring the inner knowledge ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ù…Ø¹Ø±ÙØª</span>) of the spiritual realities ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ù…Ù…Ø«ÙˆÙ„Ø§Øª</span>) behind these external rites. </p>
<p class="mainText">Bodily purification is performed with water, while the purification of the soul is accomplished through knowledge. The Noble Prophet (PBUH) states, &ldquo;There is no <span class="inlineArabic">ØµÙ„Ø§Ø©</span> (prayer) without <span class="inlineArabic">Ø·Ù‡Ø§Ø±Ø©</span> (purity).&rdquo; </p>
<p class="mainText">
  <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù„ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> (Ablution) is a method for the evacuation of gross matter ( <span class="inlineArabic">ÙØ¶Ù„Ø§Øª Ú¾Ø§Ø¨Ø·Ûƒ</span>) from the body.
</p>
<p class="mainText">
  <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù„ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> signifies the recognition of the Huduud (ranks/limits) of the Imam ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù…Ø§Ù… Ø¹Ù„ÛŒÛ Ø§Ù„Ø³Ù„Ø§Ù…</span>), and the <span class="inlineArabic">ØµÙ„Ø§Ø©</span> (prayer) is evidence of establishing oneself within the Da&lsquo;wah (spiritual mission) of the Imam ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù…Ø§Ù… Ø¹Ù„ÛŒÛ Ø§Ù„Ø³Ù„Ø§Ù…</span>) through these Huduud. Since it is impossible to be established in the Imam&rsquo;s Da&lsquo;wah without recognizing the Huduud and making them one&#39;s means, <span class="inlineArabic">ØµÙ„Ø§Ø©</span> is not valid without <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span>.
</p>
<p class="mainText">Indeed, purity is half of <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§ÛŒÙ…Ø§Ù†</span> (Faith). The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) stated that whoever perfects their <span class="inlineArabic">Ø·Ù‡Ø§Ø±Ø©</span> and then leaves their house for the mosque to pray is considered to be in the state of <span class="inlineArabic">ØµÙ„Ø§Ø©</span> until their <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> is broken. This means that with <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span>, the descent of divine spiritual confirmations ( <span class="inlineArabic">ØªØ§Ø¦ÛŒØ¯Ø§Øª</span>) and illuminations ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ø´Ø±Ø§Ù‚Ø§Øª</span>) from the Imam ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù…Ø§Ù… Ø¹Ù„ÛŒÛ Ø§Ù„Ø³Ù„Ø§Ù…</span>) begins upon the believer. </p>
<p class="mainText">The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) stated that the foundation of <span class="inlineArabic">ØµÙ„Ø§Ø©</span> is built upon four things. Whoever fails to complete them, their prayer is a deception! These four things are: </p>
