<p class="mainText">Among these four essentials, perfect <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> is the very first. The perfection of <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> is achieved by repeating each step three times. Water represents the good deeds ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ø­Ø³Ù†Ø§Øª</span>) of the believers, which Allah has divided into three parts. Due to these three divisions, each part of <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> is repeated three times. For the same reason, one is instructed to drink water in three gulps. Likewise, knowledge is also divided into the three parts of <span class="inlineArabic">Ø´Ø±ÛŒØ¹Øª</span> (Law), <span class="inlineArabic">ØªØ£ÙˆÛŒÙ„</span> (Esoteric Interpretation), and <span class="inlineArabic">Ø­Ù‚Ø§Ø¦Ù‚</span> (Ultimate Realities). Washing or wiping each limb three times signifies the recognition of the three Huduud of the Da&lsquo;wah (Spiritual Mission): <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù„Ù†Ø§Ø·Ù‚</span> (The Speaker-Prophet), <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù„Ø§Ø³Ø§Ø³</span> (The Foundation), and <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù„Ø¥Ù…Ø§Ù…</span> (The Imam). </p>
<h2 class="mainText">(Purity)&nbsp;</h2>
<p class="mainText">When a believer performs <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> once, they come into the sight of the Dai al-Waqt (Summoner of the Age), meaning the Dai perceives their pure intention ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ø­Ø³Ù† Ù†ÛŒØª</span>). When they repeat the action a second time, Allah grants them double the reward, and they enter the <em>Wilaayah</em> (Authority) of the Imam al-Zamaan (Imam of the Time), through which they attain spiritual purity ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ø¨Ø§Ø·Ù†ÛŒ Ø·ÛØ§Ø±Øª</span>). When they perform the act a third time, the Prophet ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù„Ù¾ÛŒØºÙ…Ø¨Ø± Ø¹Ù„ÛŒÛ Ø§Ù„Ø³Ù„Ø§Ù…</span> - The Speaker) declares, &ldquo;This is my <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> and the <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> of the Prophets over whom I am the Master!&rdquo; This means they have reached the rank of &#39;Perfection&#39; ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ú©Ù…Ø§Ù„</span>). </p>
<p class="mainText">Purifying each limb three times indicates that when the believer completes their obligatory duties three times&mdash;that is, when they achieve the perfect knowledge of the Dai al-Waqt, the Imam al-Zamaan, and the Naatiq ash-Shari&lsquo;ah (The Speaker of the Law)&mdash;their rank is elevated, and they become included among the Huduud ad-Din (Ranks of Religion). In essence, <span class="inlineArabic">ÙˆØ¶ÙˆØ¡</span> is a means of being included among the Huduud of the Imam ( <span class="inlineArabic">Ø§Ù…Ø§Ù… Ø¹Ù„ÛŒÛ Ø§Ù„Ø³Ù„Ø§Ù…</span>). </p>
